## 3. Complete Logic Flow

### 3.1 Plan Generation (Full Pipeline)

```
Client → POST /api/v1/plans/generate
           ↓
        GeneratePlanRequest validated (Pydantic)
           ↓
        generate_plan_task.delay(payload)  → Celery → Redis broker
           ↓ (async)
        returns JobResponse { job_id, status=pending }
        
Worker picks up task:
        generate_plan_task(payload)
           ↓
        GeneratePlanRequest.model_validate(payload)
           ↓
        asyncio.run(plan_orchestrator.generate_plan(...))
           ↓
        [STAGE 0] Detect mode: A / B / C
           ↓
  MODE A (profile only):
        _default_exercise_pool() → get_default_exercises(goal, equipment, exp_level, injuries)
        _default_diet_notes(user_profile)
        
  MODE B/C (with YouTube):
        _fetch_transcripts(urls)        → YouTubeService.fetch_many() [parallel, 12k guard]
        _classify_videos()              → SummarizerService.classify_video() [Ollama]
        _collect_by_label(workout/diet) → concat transcripts by category
        ollama_client.extract_exercises(workout_text) → ExerciseLibrary
        safety_engine.filter_exercises(injuries, equipment)  [fallback to default if empty]
        _extract_diet_guidance(diet_transcripts)  → ollama_client.generate_text(prompt)

        [STAGE 4] capacity_engine.calculate_score(biometrics, strength, physical_activity, body_composition?)
        [STAGE 5] _compute_body_metrics(user_profile, capacity_score) → BodyMetrics
        [STAGE 7] _build_base_week(safe_exercises) → WeeklySchedule (Mon/Wed/Fri chunks)
        [STAGE 7b] scheduler.build_weekly_plan() → WeeklyPlan + roadmap
        [STAGE 8] progression_engine.apply_progression(base_week, 4 weeks, capacity_score) → List[WeeklySchedule]

        Returns FitnessPlan { title, weeks, body_metrics, diet_notes, body_composition, roadmap }
           ↓
        _persist_plan(job_id, "done", plan_dict)
        
Client polls: GET /api/v1/plans/job/{job_id}
           ↓
        celery_app.AsyncResult(job_id).state → JobStatusResponse { status, result? }
        
Client downloads: GET /api/v1/plans/job/{job_id}/pdf
           ↓
        FitnessPlan.model_validate(result) → pdf_architect.render_plan(plan) → bytes stream
```

### 3.2 Vision Body Composition Analysis

```
Client → POST /api/v1/vision/analyze-body
         (multipart: front + side? + back?, X-Vision-Consent: true, height_cm, gender)
           ↓
        Consent check (HTTP 451 if missing)
        MIME / size / resolution validation per image
           ↓
        body_composition_service.analyze(images, height_cm, gender)
           ↓ [asyncio.to_thread for each image]
        Per image: _InferenceEngine.analyse_one(image_bytes, height_cm, gender)
          ├── _decode() → BGR numpy (validates 10MB max, 200px min)
          ├── _extract_features() → MobileNetV2 global-avg-pool (1280-dim features)
          │     └── _features_to_muscle() → MuscleLevel + confidence
          └── _landmark_metrics() → MediaPipe Pose (context manager, static_image_mode=2)
                ├── RFM body fat: rfm_k - (20 * height / waist_circ)  [male k=64, female k=76]
                ├── V-taper: shoulder_cm / hip_cm
                ├── Posture: shoulder tilt heuristic
                └── SWR: calculate_shoulder_waist_ratio(landmarks, w, h)
                      → (shoulder_px, waist_px, ratio, SWRCategory)
           ↓
        _fuse(valid_results): ensemble avg scalars, majority-vote categories
           ↓
        Returns BodyComposition Pydantic model
```

