## 4. Key Formulas

### BMI
```
BMI = weight_kg / (height_m)²
```

### BMR (Mifflin-St Jeor)
```
Male:   10 * weight_kg + 6.25 * height_cm - 5 * age + 5
Female: 10 * weight_kg + 6.25 * height_cm - 5 * age - 161
```

### TDEE
```
TDEE = BMR × PAL_factor
PAL: sedentary=1.20, lightly_active=1.375, moderately_active=1.55, very_active=1.725, extra_active=1.90
```

### Calorie Target
```
calorie_target = max(1200, TDEE + goal_delta)
Goal deltas: weight_loss=-500, muscle_gain=+300, strength_gain=+200, endurance/flexibility/general=0
```

### Protein Target (Orchestrator internal)
```
protein_factor = 1.6 + (0.6 × (capacity_score - 0.5))  → range 1.6–2.2 g/kg
protein_g = max(50, weight_kg × protein_factor)
fat_g = calorie_target × 0.25 / 9
carbs_g = max(0, (calorie_target - protein_g×4 - fat_g×9) / 4)
```

### Ideal Weight (Devine Formula)
```
height_over_152 = max(0, height_cm - 152.4)
Male:   ideal_kg = 50 + 2.3 × (height_over_152 / 2.54)
Female: ideal_kg = 45.5 + 2.3 × (height_over_152 / 2.54)
```

### Capacity Score
```
Base = strength_score (from pushup/squat/situp ratios)
  + activity_bonus (from hours/day: 0–0.15)
  - BMI_penalty (BMI 25–30: -0.05; 30+: -0.10)
  + muscle_bonus (MuscleLevel: high=+0.05, very_high=+0.10)
  + SWR_bonus (athletic=+0.08, overfat=-0.05)
Final = clamp(base_score, 0.50, 1.50)
```

### RFM Body Fat
```
Male:   rfm = 64 - (20 × height_cm / waist_circumference_cm)
Female: rfm = 76 - (20 × height_cm / waist_circumference_cm)
clamped: [3%, 50%]
```

### Shoulder-to-Waist Ratio (SWR)
```
swr = shoulder_width_px / waist_width_px   (hip landmark used as waist proxy)
Categories: swr < 1.0 → OVERFAT, 1.0–1.2 → BALANCED, > 1.2 → ATHLETIC
```

### MobileNetV2 Muscle Proxy Score
```
features = MobileNetV2 GlobalAvgPool (1280-dim)
hi = mean(|features[640:]|)
lo = mean(|features[:640]|)
score = hi / (hi + lo)
Thresholds: ≥0.70 → Very High, ≥0.52 → High, ≥0.34 → Moderate, else → Low
```

### Progressive Overload (Progression Engine)
```
For each week w (1-4):
  reps_multiplier   = 1.0 + (w × 0.05 × capacity_score)
  weight_multiplier = 1.0 + (w × 0.025 × capacity_score)
  Each set: reps = round(base_reps × reps_multiplier), weight_kg = base_weight × weight_multiplier
```

